  "summary": "Surrealist techniques involving rubbing textures onto paper (frottage) and scraping paint layers (grattage).",
  "description": "Frottage involves placing paper over textured surfaces and rubbing with graphite to create relief patterns, while grattage involves scraping through layers of wet paint to reveal textures underneath. Developed by Max Ernst, these techniques embraced chance and automatism in artmaking.",
